-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4.
-- PART 12ZC, STATUTORY SHARED PARENTAL PAY, ss 171ZU to 171ZZ5 (src:3718-4016).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively.  The source is a plain-text rendering made by a converter
-- script; it is not the official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text".
--
-- How to read a result (the rule of 2026-10-29):
--   JUST FALSE / JUST TRUE : the text says no / yes in its own words (each "no" branch quotes them).
--   NOTHING                : not covered (each branch says why: silent, list not closed, includes,
--                            undefined term, points outside the text, limited by its own wording).
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Money is a NUMBER in pounds sterling.  Rates, periods and lengths that regulations supply are
-- INPUTS.  Dates are `Date day month year`.

§ `Part 12ZC -- Statutory shared parental pay`

§§ `s 171ZU Entitlement: birth`
-- GENERATED by work/gen_zc.py from the paragraph list in that script: condition sets of Part 12ZC and the
-- entitlement wrappers that carry the regulations gate.  Edit the script, not this part.

-- Nouns: the facts of the claimant mother's case that s 171ZU(2) reads.  "Prescribed" conditions are facts the person states;
-- the prescribed length and the lower earnings limit are figures regulations supply.

DECLARE `s 171ZU(2) the claimant mother's case` HAS
    `(a) the claimant mother and P satisfy prescribed conditions as to caring or intending to care for the child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(b)(i) P satisfies prescribed conditions as to employment or self-employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(b)(ii) P satisfies prescribed conditions as to having earnings of a prescribed amount for a prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(b)(iii) P satisfies prescribed conditions as to relationship either with the child or with the claimant mother` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(c) weeks of continuous employment ending with the prescribed week` IS A NUMBER
    `(c) the prescribed length of continuous employment in weeks` IS A NUMBER
    `(d) at the end of that prescribed week the claimant mother was entitled to be in that employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(e) normal weekly earnings in pounds for the prescribed period ending with the prescribed week` IS A NUMBER
    `(f) regulations so provide that the person continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(f) the claimant mother continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(g) the claimant mother became entitled to statutory maternity pay by reference to the birth of the child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(h) the claimant mother satisfies prescribed conditions as to the reduction of the duration of the maternity pay period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(i)(i) the claimant mother has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks she would be entitled to claim if the entitlement were fully exercised` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(i)(ii) the claimant mother has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks she intends to claim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(i)(iii) the claimant mother has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks in respect of which P intends to claim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(j) the claimant mother has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the period or periods during which she intends to claim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(k)(i) a notice under paragraph (i) or (j) is given by such time as may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(k)(ii) a notice under paragraph (i) or (j) satisfies prescribed conditions as to form and content` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(l) P consents to the extent of the claimant mother's intended claim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(m) it is the claimant mother's intention to care for the child during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to her` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(n) the claimant mother is absent from work during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to her` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(o) the person is an employee within the meaning of the Employment Rights Act 1996` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(o) the claimant mother's absence from work during each such week is absence on shared parental leave` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 171ZU(2) "The conditions are": every paragraph must be satisfied.  (f)/(g)-type paragraphs that bite only "if regulations so provide"
-- and the "where ... an employee" paragraph are read as: no such regulation (or not an employee) means nothing to fail.
-- src:3721 | (2) The conditions are—
-- src:3722 | (a) that the claimant mother and another person (“P”) satisfy prescribed conditions as to caring or intending to care for the child;
-- src:3723 | (b) that P satisfies prescribed conditions—
-- src:3724 | (i) as to employment or self-employment,
-- src:3725 | (ii) as to having earnings of a prescribed amount for a prescribed period, and
-- src:3726 | (iii) as to relationship either with the child or with the claimant mother;
-- src:3727 | (c) that the claimant mother has been in employed earner's employment with an employer for a continuous period of at least the prescribed length ending with a prescribed week;
-- src:3728 | (d) that at the end of that prescribed week the claimant mother was entitled to be in that employment;
-- src:3729 | (e) that the claimant mother's normal weekly earnings for a prescribed period ending with a prescribed week are not less than the lower earnings limit in force under section 5(1)(a) at the end of that week;
-- src:3730 | (f) if regulations so provide, that the claimant mother continues in employed earner's employment (whether or not with the employer by reference to whom the condition in paragraph (c) is satisfied) until a prescribed time;
-- src:3731 | (g) that the claimant mother became entitled to statutory maternity pay by reference to the birth of the child;
-- src:3732 | (h) that the claimant mother satisfies prescribed conditions as to the reduction of the duration of the maternity pay period;
-- src:3733 | (i) that the claimant mother has given the person who will be liable to pay statutory shared parental pay to her notice of—
-- src:3734 | (i) the number of weeks in respect of which she would be entitled to claim statutory shared parental pay in respect of the child if the entitlement were fully exercised (disregarding for these purposes any intention of P to claim statutory shared parental pay in respect of the child),
-- src:3735 | (ii) the number of weeks in respect of which she intends to claim statutory shared parental pay, and
-- src:3736 | (iii) the number of weeks in respect of which P intends to claim statutory shared parental pay;
-- src:3737 | (j) that the claimant mother has given the person who will be liable to pay statutory shared parental pay to her notice of the period or periods during which she intends to claim statutory shared parental pay in respect of the child;
-- src:3738 | (k) that a notice under paragraph (i) or (j)—
-- src:3739 | (i) is given by such time as may be prescribed, and
-- src:3740 | (ii) satisfies prescribed conditions as to form and content;
-- src:3741 | (l) that P consents to the extent of the claimant mother's intended claim for statutory shared parental pay;
-- src:3742 | (m) that it is the claimant mother's intention to care for the child during each week in respect of which statutory shared parental pay is paid to her;
-- src:3743 | (n) that the claimant mother is absent from work during each week in respect of which statutory shared parental pay is paid to her;
-- src:3744 | (o) that, where she is an employee within the meaning of the Employment Rights Act 1996, the claimant mother's absence from work during each such week is absence on shared parental leave.
@ref s 171ZU(2) (src:3721-3744)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 171ZU(2) the claimant mother's case`
      `s 5(1)(a) the lower earnings limit in force at the time in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 171ZU(2) all the conditions are satisfied` MEANS
        (facts's `(a) the claimant mother and P satisfy prescribed conditions as to caring or intending to care for the child`)   -- (a)
    AND (facts's `(b)(i) P satisfies prescribed conditions as to employment or self-employment`) AND (facts's `(b)(ii) P satisfies prescribed conditions as to having earnings of a prescribed amount for a prescribed period`) AND (facts's `(b)(iii) P satisfies prescribed conditions as to relationship either with the child or with the claimant mother`)   -- (b)
    AND (facts's `(c) weeks of continuous employment ending with the prescribed week`) AT LEAST (facts's `(c) the prescribed length of continuous employment in weeks`)   -- (c)
    AND (facts's `(d) at the end of that prescribed week the claimant mother was entitled to be in that employment`)   -- (d)
    AND (facts's `(e) normal weekly earnings in pounds for the prescribed period ending with the prescribed week`) AT LEAST `s 5(1)(a) the lower earnings limit in force at the time in pounds`   -- (e)
    AND ((NOT (facts's `(f) regulations so provide that the person continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time`)) OR (facts's `(f) the claimant mother continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time`))   -- (f)
    AND (facts's `(g) the claimant mother became entitled to statutory maternity pay by reference to the birth of the child`)   -- (g)
    AND (facts's `(h) the claimant mother satisfies prescribed conditions as to the reduction of the duration of the maternity pay period`)   -- (h)
    AND (facts's `(i)(i) the claimant mother has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks she would be entitled to claim if the entitlement were fully exercised`) AND (facts's `(i)(ii) the claimant mother has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks she intends to claim`) AND (facts's `(i)(iii) the claimant mother has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks in respect of which P intends to claim`)   -- (i)
    AND (facts's `(j) the claimant mother has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the period or periods during which she intends to claim`)   -- (j)
    AND (facts's `(k)(i) a notice under paragraph (i) or (j) is given by such time as may be prescribed`) AND (facts's `(k)(ii) a notice under paragraph (i) or (j) satisfies prescribed conditions as to form and content`)   -- (k)
    AND (facts's `(l) P consents to the extent of the claimant mother's intended claim`)   -- (l)
    AND (facts's `(m) it is the claimant mother's intention to care for the child during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to her`)   -- (m)
    AND (facts's `(n) the claimant mother is absent from work during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to her`)   -- (n)
    AND ((NOT (facts's `(o) the person is an employee within the meaning of the Employment Rights Act 1996`)) OR (facts's `(o) the claimant mother's absence from work during each such week is absence on shared parental leave`))   -- (o)

