-- a condition in the person's case, the text alone cannot answer.  A failed "where" is counted as the text's no (reading (a), for a lawyer).
-- src:3745 | (3) Regulations may provide that, where all the conditions in subsection (4) are satisfied in relation to a person (“the claimant”), the claimant is to be entitled in accordance with the following provisions of this Part to payments to be known as “statutory shared parental pay”.
@ref s 171ZU(3) (src:3745)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 171ZU(4) the claimant's case`
      `s 5(1)(a) the lower earnings limit in force at the time in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `regulations under s 171ZU(3) provide that the claimant is entitled where the conditions in subsection (4) are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 171ZW(1)(a) regulations disapply or modify a condition in the claimant's case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
