-- (5) Regulations may provide for the determination of the extent of entitlement and for when the pay is payable:
-- a power, nothing to encode.

-- Nouns for (6): which maternity payment the mother (or M) was paid.
DECLARE `s 171ZU(6) kind of maternity payment` IS ONE OF
    `s 171ZU(6) maternity allowance`
    `s 171ZU(6) statutory maternity pay`

-- (7)(a) "'relevant week' means ... where maternity allowance is payable to a mother, a week or part of a week falling before
-- the time at which the mother takes action that is treated by regulations as constituting ... her return to work".
-- "Week" is the s 122(1) week: seven days beginning with Sunday (the core's first week convention).  A part-week counts, at
-- either end.  The weeks are counted from the first day on which the allowance is payable.
-- src:3784 | (7) In subsection (6)(a) “relevant week” means—
-- src:3785 | (a) where maternity allowance is payable to a mother, a week or part of a week falling before the time at which the mother takes action that is treated by regulations as constituting for the purposes of this section her return to work;
-- src:3787 | For these purposes “week” has the meaning given by section 122(1), in relation to maternity allowance, or the meaning given by section 165(8), in relation to statutory maternity pay.
@ref s 171ZU(7)(a) (src:3784-3787)
GIVEN payable IS A Period
      action IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 171ZU(7)(a) the number of relevant weeks of maternity allowance` MEANS
    IF action AT MOST payable's `the first day`
    THEN 0
    ELSE (FLOOR ((lastSerial MINUS firstSunday) DIVIDED BY 7)) PLUS 1
    WHERE
        lastSerial MEANS IF action GREATER THAN payable's `the last day` THEN Day (payable's `the last day`) ELSE (Day action) MINUS 1
        firstSunday MEANS (Day (payable's `the first day`)) MINUS (`Weekday of` (payable's `the first day`))

-- (7)(b) "where statutory maternity pay is payable to a mother, a week falling before the week in which the mother takes action
-- that is so treated."  "Week" is the s 165(8) week: seven days beginning with the day of the week on which the maternity pay
-- period begins (the core's fourth week convention).  Only whole weeks before the week of the action count.
-- src:3784 | (7) In subsection (6)(a) “relevant week” means—
-- src:3786 | (b) where statutory maternity pay is payable to a mother, a week falling before the week in which the mother takes action that is so treated.
-- src:3787 | For these purposes “week” has the meaning given by section 122(1), in relation to maternity allowance, or the meaning given by section 165(8), in relation to statutory maternity pay.
@ref s 171ZU(7)(b) (src:3784-3787)
GIVEN period IS A Period
      action IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 171ZU(7)(b) the number of relevant weeks of statutory maternity pay` MEANS
    IF action AT MOST period's `the first day`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF wholeWeeksBefore GREATER THAN weeksInPeriod THEN weeksInPeriod ELSE wholeWeeksBefore
    WHERE
        wholeWeeksBefore MEANS FLOOR (((Day action) MINUS (Day (period's `the first day`))) DIVIDED BY 7)
        weeksInPeriod MEANS FLOOR ((((Day (period's `the last day`)) MINUS (Day (period's `the first day`))) PLUS 1) DIVIDED BY 7)

-- (8)(b) "In determining the number of weeks for the purposes of subsection (6)(b) ... a part of a week is to be treated as a week."
-- src:3788 | (8) In determining the number of weeks for the purposes of subsection (6)(b)—
-- src:3789 | (a) “week” has the same meaning as in subsection (7), and
-- src:3790 | (b) a part of a week is to be treated as a week.
@ref s 171ZU(8) (src:3788-3790)
GIVEN weeks IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 171ZU(8) the number of weeks counting a part of a week as a week` MEANS
    CEILING weeks

-- (6) "Provision under subsection (5)(a) is to secure that the number of weeks in respect of which a person is entitled to
-- payments of statutory shared parental pay in respect of a child does not exceed the number of weeks of the maternity pay period
-- reduced by (a) where the mother ... takes action that is treated by regulations as constituting ... her return to work without
-- satisfying conditions prescribed under subsection (2)(h) or (4)(i) (i) the number of relevant weeks in respect of which
-- maternity allowance or statutory maternity pay is payable to the mother, or (ii) if that number of relevant weeks is less than a
-- number prescribed by regulations, that prescribed number of weeks, or (b) except where paragraph (a) applies, the number of weeks
-- to which the maternity allowance period is reduced by virtue of section 35(3A) or, as the case may be, the maternity pay period is
-- reduced by virtue of section 165(3A)."  The weeks of the period reduced "by" a number are the period's weeks less that number.
-- Fork F2: for maternity allowance the text names only "the maternity pay period" as the starting figure; the maternity allowance
-- period is taken for that case, as paragraph (b) does.  The two reduced-to figures come from ss 35(3A) and 165(3A) (seam S27).
-- src:3779 | (6) Provision under subsection (5)(a) is to secure that the number of weeks in respect of which a person is entitled to payments of statutory shared parental pay in respect of a child does not exceed the number of weeks of the maternity pay period reduced by—
-- src:3780 | (a) where the mother of the child takes action that is treated by regulations as constituting for the purposes of this section her return to work without satisfying conditions prescribed under subsection (2)(h) or, as the case may be, subsection (4)(i)—
-- src:3781 | (i) the number of relevant weeks in respect of which maternity allowance or statutory maternity pay is payable to the mother, or
-- src:3782 | (ii) if that number of relevant weeks is less than a number prescribed by regulations, that prescribed number of weeks, or
-- src:3783 | (b) except where paragraph (a) applies, the number of weeks to which the maternity allowance period is reduced by virtue of section 35(3A) or, as the case may be, the maternity pay period is reduced by virtue of section 165(3A).
@ref s 171ZU(6) (src:3779-3783)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 171ZU(6) kind of maternity payment`
      `s 165(1) the maternity pay period` IS A Period
      `s 35(2) the maternity allowance period` IS A Period
      `the mother takes action treated by regulations as her return to work without satisfying the conditions prescribed under subsection (2)(h) or (4)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of relevant weeks in respect of which maternity allowance or statutory maternity pay is payable to the mother` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of weeks prescribed by regulations` IS A NUMBER
      `s 35(3A) the number of weeks to which the maternity allowance period is reduced` IS A NUMBER
      `s 165(3A) the number of weeks to which the maternity pay period is reduced` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 171ZU(6) the greatest number of weeks of statutory shared parental pay` MEANS
    IF cap AT LEAST 0
    THEN JUST cap
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the reduction would exceed the weeks of the period, and the text does not say what then
    WHERE
        weeksOf MEANS GIVEN p IS A Period YIELD (((Day (p's `the last day`)) MINUS (Day (p's `the first day`))) PLUS 1) DIVIDED BY 7
        base MEANS
            CONSIDER kind
            WHEN `s 171ZU(6) maternity allowance` THEN weeksOf `s 35(2) the maternity allowance period`
            WHEN `s 171ZU(6) statutory maternity pay` THEN weeksOf `s 165(1) the maternity pay period`
        reduction MEANS
            IF `the mother takes action treated by regulations as her return to work without satisfying the conditions prescribed under subsection (2)(h) or (4)(i)`
            THEN (IF `the number of relevant weeks in respect of which maternity allowance or statutory maternity pay is payable to the mother` LESS THAN `the number of weeks prescribed by regulations`
                  THEN `the number of weeks prescribed by regulations`
                  ELSE `the number of relevant weeks in respect of which maternity allowance or statutory maternity pay is payable to the mother`)
            ELSE (CONSIDER kind
                  WHEN `s 171ZU(6) maternity allowance` THEN `s 171ZU(8) the number of weeks counting a part of a week as a week` `s 35(3A) the number of weeks to which the maternity allowance period is reduced`
                  WHEN `s 171ZU(6) statutory maternity pay` THEN `s 171ZU(8) the number of weeks counting a part of a week as a week` `s 165(3A) the number of weeks to which the maternity pay period is reduced`)
        cap MEANS base MINUS reduction

-- (9) "Provision under subsection (5)(a) is to secure that, where two persons are entitled to payments ... in respect of a child,
-- the extent of one's entitlement and the extent of the other's entitlement do not, taken together, exceed what would be available
-- to one person (see subsection (6))."
-- src:3791 | (9) Provision under subsection (5)(a) is to secure that, where two persons are entitled to payments of statutory shared parental pay in respect of a child, the extent of one's entitlement and the extent of the other's entitlement do not, taken together, exceed what would be available to one person (see subsection (6)).
@ref s 171ZU(9) (src:3791)
GIVEN `the weeks of one person's entitlement` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of the other person's entitlement` IS A NUMBER
      `the greatest number of weeks available to one person` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZU(9) the two entitlements together are within what is available to one person` MEANS
    IF `the weeks of one person's entitlement` PLUS `the weeks of the other person's entitlement` AT MOST `the greatest number of weeks available to one person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the extent of one's entitlement and the extent of the other's entitlement do not, taken together, exceed what would be available to one person"

-- (10) "Provision under subsection (5)(b) is to secure that no payment of statutory shared parental pay may be made to a person in
-- respect of a child after the end of such period as may be prescribed."  The bar bites only after the end of that period.
-- src:3792 | (10) Provision under subsection (5)(b) is to secure that no payment of statutory shared parental pay may be made to a person in respect of a child after the end of such period as may be prescribed.
@ref s 171ZU(10) (src:3792)
GIVEN `the day of the payment` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period prescribed by regulations` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZU(10) a payment may be made in respect of the child` MEANS
    IF `the day of the payment` GREATER THAN `the last day of the period prescribed by regulations`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no payment of statutory shared parental pay may be made to a person in respect of a child after the end of such period as may be prescribed"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a payment within the prescribed period is not barred here, and whether it is payable is for the other provisions

-- (11) "Provision under subsection (5)(b) is to secure that no payment of statutory shared parental pay in respect of a child may
-- be made to a person who is the mother of the child before the end of the mother's maternity pay period."  A payment on the last
-- day of the period is before the end of the period, which ends with that day.
-- src:3793 | (11) Provision under subsection (5)(b) is to secure that no payment of statutory shared parental pay in respect of a child may be made to a person who is the mother of the child before the end of the mother's maternity pay period.
@ref s 171ZU(11) (src:3793)
GIVEN `the day of the payment` IS A DATE
      `s 165(1) the maternity pay period` IS A Period
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZU(11) a payment may be made to the mother` MEANS
    IF `the day of the payment` AT MOST mpp's `the last day`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no payment of statutory shared parental pay in respect of a child may be made to a person who is the mother of the child before the end of the mother's maternity pay period"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): after the maternity pay period the bar no longer applies, and whether the pay is payable is for the other provisions
    WHERE mpp MEANS `s 165(1) the maternity pay period`

-- (13) "The conditions are (a) that V has given the person who will be liable to pay ... notice of an intention to vary the period or
-- periods ...; (b) that a notice under paragraph (a) (i) is given by such time as may be prescribed, and (ii) satisfies prescribed
-- conditions as to form and content."
-- src:3795 | (13) The conditions are—
-- src:3796 | (a) that V has given the person who will be liable to pay statutory shared parental pay to V notice of an intention to vary the period or periods during which V intends to claim statutory shared parental pay;
-- src:3797 | (b) that a notice under paragraph (a)—
-- src:3798 | (i) is given by such time as may be prescribed, and
-- src:3799 | (ii) satisfies prescribed conditions as to form and content.
@ref s 171ZU(13) (src:3795-3799)
GIVEN `V has given notice of an intention to vary the period or periods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is given by the prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice satisfies the prescribed conditions as to form and content` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 171ZU(13) the conditions for varying the period or periods are satisfied` MEANS
        `V has given notice of an intention to vary the period or periods`
    AND `the notice is given by the prescribed time`
    AND `the notice satisfies the prescribed conditions as to form and content`

-- (12) "Regulations may provide that, where the conditions in subsection (13) are satisfied in relation to a person who is entitled
-- ... (“V”), V may vary the period or periods during which V intends to claim ..., subject to complying with provision under
-- subsection (14) where that is relevant."  The permission exists as the regulations provide.
-- src:3794 | (12) Regulations may provide that, where the conditions in subsection (13) are satisfied in relation to a person who is entitled to statutory shared parental pay under subsection (1) or (3) (“V”), V may vary the period or periods during which V intends to claim statutory shared parental pay in respect of the child in question, subject to complying with provision under subsection (14) where that is relevant.
@ref s 171ZU(12) (src:3794)
GIVEN `regulations under subsection (12) provide for the variation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions in subsection (13) are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZU(12) V may vary the period or periods` MEANS
    IF NOT `regulations under subsection (12) provide for the variation`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Regulations may provide that"
    ELSE IF `the conditions in subsection (13) are satisfied`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the conditions in subsection (13) are satisfied ... V may vary" (a failed "where"; reading (a))

-- (15) "The conditions are (a) that V has given ... notice of (i) the extent to which V has exercised an entitlement ..., (ii) the extent
-- to which V intends to claim ..., (iii) the extent to which another person has exercised an entitlement ..., and (iv) the extent to
-- which another person intends to claim ...; (b) that a notice under paragraph (a) (i) is given by such time as may be prescribed, and
-- (ii) satisfies prescribed conditions as to form and content; (c) that the person who is P or, as the case may be, M in relation to V
-- consents to that variation."
-- src:3801 | (15) The conditions are—
-- src:3802 | (a) that V has given the person who will be liable to pay statutory shared parental pay to V notice of—
-- src:3803 | (i) the extent to which V has exercised an entitlement to statutory shared parental pay in respect of the child,
-- src:3804 | (ii) the extent to which V intends to claim statutory shared parental pay in respect of the child,
-- src:3805 | (iii) the extent to which another person has exercised an entitlement to statutory shared parental pay in respect of the child, and
-- src:3806 | (iv) the extent to which another person intends to claim statutory shared parental pay in respect of the child;
-- src:3807 | (b) that a notice under paragraph (a)—
-- src:3808 | (i) is given by such time as may be prescribed, and
-- src:3809 | (ii) satisfies prescribed conditions as to form and content;
-- src:3810 | (c) that the person who is P or, as the case may be, M in relation to V consents to that variation.
@ref s 171ZU(15) (src:3801-3810)
GIVEN `V has given notice of the extent to which V has exercised an entitlement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `V has given notice of the extent to which V intends to claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `V has given notice of the extent to which another person has exercised an entitlement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `V has given notice of the extent to which another person intends to claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is given by the prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice satisfies the prescribed conditions as to form and content` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person who is P or, as the case may be, M in relation to V consents to the variation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 171ZU(15) the conditions for varying the number of weeks are satisfied` MEANS
        `V has given notice of the extent to which V has exercised an entitlement`
    AND `V has given notice of the extent to which V intends to claim`
    AND `V has given notice of the extent to which another person has exercised an entitlement`
    AND `V has given notice of the extent to which another person intends to claim`
    AND `the notice is given by the prescribed time`
    AND `the notice satisfies the prescribed conditions as to form and content`
    AND `the person who is P or, as the case may be, M in relation to V consents to the variation`

-- (14) "Regulations may provide that, where the conditions in subsection (15) are satisfied ..., V may vary the number of weeks in
-- respect of which V intends to claim statutory shared parental pay."
-- src:3800 | (14) Regulations may provide that, where the conditions in subsection (15) are satisfied in relation to a person who is entitled to statutory shared parental pay under subsection (1) or (3) (“V”), V may vary the number of weeks in respect of which V intends to claim statutory shared parental pay.
@ref s 171ZU(14) (src:3800)
GIVEN `regulations under subsection (14) provide for the variation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions in subsection (15) are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZU(14) V may vary the number of weeks` MEANS
    IF NOT `regulations under subsection (14) provide for the variation`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Regulations may provide that"
    ELSE IF `the conditions in subsection (15) are satisfied`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the conditions in subsection (15) are satisfied ... V may vary" (a failed "where"; reading (a))

-- (16) "A person's entitlement to statutory shared parental pay under this section is not affected by the birth of more than one
-- child as a result of the same pregnancy."  The answer is the same for one child or several.
-- src:3811 | (16) A person's entitlement to statutory shared parental pay under this section is not affected by the birth of more than one child as a result of the same pregnancy.
@ref s 171ZU(16) (src:3811)
GIVEN `the person is entitled under subsection (1) or (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the number of children born as a result of the same pregnancy` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZU(16) the entitlement after the birth of more than one child` MEANS
    IF `the number of children born as a result of the same pregnancy` AT LEAST 1
    THEN `the person is entitled under subsection (1) or (3)`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): there is no birth to speak of

§§ `s 171ZV Entitlement: adoption`
-- GENERATED by work/gen_zc.py from the paragraph list in that script: condition sets of Part 12ZC and the
-- entitlement wrappers that carry the regulations gate.  Edit the script, not this part.

-- Nouns: the facts of the claimant A's case that s 171ZV(2) reads.  "Prescribed" conditions are facts the person states;
-- the prescribed length and the lower earnings limit are figures regulations supply.

DECLARE `s 171ZV(2) the claimant A's case` HAS
    `(a) claimant A and X satisfy prescribed conditions as to caring or intending to care for the child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(b)(i) X satisfies prescribed conditions as to employment or self-employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(b)(ii) X satisfies prescribed conditions as to having earnings of a prescribed amount for a prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(b)(iii) X satisfies prescribed conditions as to relationship either with the child or with claimant A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(c) weeks of continuous employment ending with the prescribed week` IS A NUMBER
    `(c) the prescribed length of continuous employment in weeks` IS A NUMBER
    `(d) at the end of that prescribed week claimant A was entitled to be in that employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(e) normal weekly earnings in pounds for the prescribed period ending with the prescribed week` IS A NUMBER
    `(f) regulations so provide that the person continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(f) claimant A continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(g) claimant A became entitled to statutory adoption pay by reference to the placement for adoption of the child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(h) claimant A satisfies prescribed conditions as to the reduction of the duration of the adoption pay period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(i)(i) claimant A has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks claimant A would be entitled to claim if the entitlement were fully exercised` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(i)(ii) claimant A has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks claimant A intends to claim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(i)(iii) claimant A has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks in respect of which X intends to claim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(j) claimant A has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the period or periods during which claimant A intends to claim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(k)(i) a notice under paragraph (i) or (j) is given by such time as may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(k)(ii) a notice under paragraph (i) or (j) satisfies prescribed conditions as to form and content` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(l) X consents to the extent of claimant A's intended claim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(m) it is claimant A's intention to care for the child during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to claimant A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(n) claimant A is absent from work during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to claimant A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(o) the person is an employee within the meaning of the Employment Rights Act 1996` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(o) claimant A's absence from work during each such week is absence on shared parental leave` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 171ZV(2) "The conditions are": every paragraph must be satisfied.  (f)/(g)-type paragraphs that bite only "if regulations so provide"
-- and the "where ... an employee" paragraph are read as: no such regulation (or not an employee) means nothing to fail.
-- src:3814 | (2) The conditions are—
-- src:3815 | (a) that claimant A and another person (“X”) satisfy prescribed conditions as to caring or intending to care for the child;
-- src:3816 | (b) that X satisfies prescribed conditions—
-- src:3817 | (i) as to employment or self-employment,
-- src:3818 | (ii) as to having earnings of a prescribed amount for a prescribed period, and
-- src:3819 | (iii) as to relationship either with the child or with claimant A;
-- src:3820 | (c) that claimant A has been in employed earner's employment with an employer for a continuous period of at least the prescribed length ending with a prescribed week;
-- src:3821 | (d) that at the end of that prescribed week claimant A was entitled to be in that employment;
-- src:3822 | (e) that claimant A's normal weekly earnings for a prescribed period ending with a prescribed week are not less than the lower earnings limit in force under section 5(1)(a) at the end of that week;
-- src:3823 | (f) if regulations so provide, that claimant A continues in employed earner's employment (whether or not with the employer by reference to whom the condition in paragraph (c) is satisfied) until a prescribed time;
-- src:3824 | (g) that claimant A became entitled to statutory adoption pay by reference to the placement for adoption of the child;
-- src:3825 | (h) that claimant A satisfies prescribed conditions as to the reduction of the duration of the adoption pay period;
-- src:3826 | (i) that claimant A has given the person who will be liable to pay statutory shared parental pay to claimant A notice of—
-- src:3827 | (i) the number of weeks in respect of which claimant A would be entitled to claim statutory shared parental pay in respect of the child if the entitlement were fully exercised (disregarding for these purposes any intention of X to claim statutory shared parental pay in respect of the child),
-- src:3828 | (ii) the number of weeks in respect of which claimant A intends to claim statutory shared parental pay, and
-- src:3829 | (iii) the number of weeks in respect of which X intends to claim statutory shared parental pay;
-- src:3830 | (j) that claimant A has given the person who will be liable to pay statutory shared parental pay to claimant A notice of the period or periods during which claimant A intends to claim statutory shared parental pay in respect of the child;
-- src:3831 | (k) that a notice under paragraph (i) or (j)—
-- src:3832 | (i) is given by such time as may be prescribed, and
-- src:3833 | (ii) satisfies prescribed conditions as to form and content;
-- src:3834 | (l) that X consents to the extent of claimant A's intended claim for statutory shared parental pay;
-- src:3835 | (m) that it is claimant A's intention to care for the child during each week in respect of which statutory shared parental pay is paid to claimant A;
-- src:3836 | (n) that claimant A is absent from work during each week in respect of which statutory shared parental pay is paid to claimant A;
-- src:3837 | (o) that, where claimant A is an employee within the meaning of the Employment Rights Act 1996, claimant A's absence from work during each such week is absence on shared parental leave.
@ref s 171ZV(2) (src:3814-3837)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 171ZV(2) the claimant A's case`
      `s 5(1)(a) the lower earnings limit in force at the time in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 171ZV(2) all the conditions are satisfied` MEANS
        (facts's `(a) claimant A and X satisfy prescribed conditions as to caring or intending to care for the child`)   -- (a)
    AND (facts's `(b)(i) X satisfies prescribed conditions as to employment or self-employment`) AND (facts's `(b)(ii) X satisfies prescribed conditions as to having earnings of a prescribed amount for a prescribed period`) AND (facts's `(b)(iii) X satisfies prescribed conditions as to relationship either with the child or with claimant A`)   -- (b)
    AND (facts's `(c) weeks of continuous employment ending with the prescribed week`) AT LEAST (facts's `(c) the prescribed length of continuous employment in weeks`)   -- (c)
    AND (facts's `(d) at the end of that prescribed week claimant A was entitled to be in that employment`)   -- (d)
    AND (facts's `(e) normal weekly earnings in pounds for the prescribed period ending with the prescribed week`) AT LEAST `s 5(1)(a) the lower earnings limit in force at the time in pounds`   -- (e)
    AND ((NOT (facts's `(f) regulations so provide that the person continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time`)) OR (facts's `(f) claimant A continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time`))   -- (f)
    AND (facts's `(g) claimant A became entitled to statutory adoption pay by reference to the placement for adoption of the child`)   -- (g)
    AND (facts's `(h) claimant A satisfies prescribed conditions as to the reduction of the duration of the adoption pay period`)   -- (h)
    AND (facts's `(i)(i) claimant A has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks claimant A would be entitled to claim if the entitlement were fully exercised`) AND (facts's `(i)(ii) claimant A has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks claimant A intends to claim`) AND (facts's `(i)(iii) claimant A has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks in respect of which X intends to claim`)   -- (i)
    AND (facts's `(j) claimant A has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the period or periods during which claimant A intends to claim`)   -- (j)
    AND (facts's `(k)(i) a notice under paragraph (i) or (j) is given by such time as may be prescribed`) AND (facts's `(k)(ii) a notice under paragraph (i) or (j) satisfies prescribed conditions as to form and content`)   -- (k)
    AND (facts's `(l) X consents to the extent of claimant A's intended claim`)   -- (l)
    AND (facts's `(m) it is claimant A's intention to care for the child during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to claimant A`)   -- (m)
    AND (facts's `(n) claimant A is absent from work during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to claimant A`)   -- (n)
    AND ((NOT (facts's `(o) the person is an employee within the meaning of the Employment Rights Act 1996`)) OR (facts's `(o) claimant A's absence from work during each such week is absence on shared parental leave`))   -- (o)

-- s 171ZV(1): "Regulations may provide that, where all the conditions in 171ZV(2) are satisfied ... is to be entitled".
-- READING B (fork F1): the Act states the conditions and the entitlement exists as the regulations provide.  The gate
-- `regulations under s 171ZV(1) provide that claimant A is entitled where the conditions in subsection (2) are satisfied` is an input; if it is false, or if regulations under s 171ZW(1)(a) disapply or modify
-- a condition in the person's case, the text alone cannot answer.  A failed "where" is counted as the text's no (reading (a), for a lawyer).
-- src:3813 | (1) Regulations may provide that, where all the conditions in subsection (2) are satisfied in relation to a person with whom a child is, or is expected to be, placed for adoption under the law of any part of the United Kingdom (“claimant A”), claimant A is to be entitled in accordance with the following provisions of this Part to payments to be known as “statutory shared parental pay”.
@ref s 171ZV(1) (src:3813)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 171ZV(2) the claimant A's case`
      `s 5(1)(a) the lower earnings limit in force at the time in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `regulations under s 171ZV(1) provide that claimant A is entitled where the conditions in subsection (2) are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 171ZW(1)(a) regulations disapply or modify a condition in the claimant A's case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZV(1) claimant A is entitled to statutory shared parental pay` MEANS
    IF NOT `regulations under s 171ZV(1) provide that claimant A is entitled where the conditions in subsection (2) are satisfied`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Regulations may provide that" -- the entitlement exists only as regulations provide
    ELSE IF `s 171ZW(1)(a) regulations disapply or modify a condition in the claimant A's case`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 171ZW(1)(a) lets regulations disapply or modify the conditions in prescribed cases
         ELSE IF `s 171ZV(2) all the conditions are satisfied` facts `s 5(1)(a) the lower earnings limit in force at the time in pounds`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Regulations may provide that, where all the conditions in subsection (2) are satisfied in relation to a person with whom a child is, or is expected to be, placed for adoption under the law of any part of the United Kingdom (“claimant A”), claimant A is to be entitled" (a failed "where"; reading (a))

-- Nouns: the facts of the claimant B's case that s 171ZV(4) reads.  "Prescribed" conditions are facts the person states;
-- the prescribed length and the lower earnings limit are figures regulations supply.

DECLARE `s 171ZV(4) the claimant B's case` HAS
    `(a) claimant B and Y satisfy prescribed conditions as to caring or intending to care for the child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(b)(i) claimant B satisfies prescribed conditions as to relationship with the child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(b)(ii) claimant B satisfies prescribed conditions as to relationship with Y` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(c)(i) Y satisfies prescribed conditions as to employment or self-employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(c)(ii) Y satisfies prescribed conditions as to having earnings of a prescribed amount for a prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(d) weeks of continuous employment ending with the prescribed week` IS A NUMBER
    `(d) the prescribed length of continuous employment in weeks` IS A NUMBER
    `(e) at the end of that prescribed week claimant B was entitled to be in that employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(f) normal weekly earnings in pounds for the prescribed period ending with the prescribed week` IS A NUMBER
    `(g) regulations so provide that the person continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(g) claimant B continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(h) Y became entitled to statutory adoption pay by reference to the placement for adoption of the child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(i) Y satisfies prescribed conditions as to the reduction of the duration of the adoption pay period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(j)(i) claimant B has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks claimant B would be entitled to claim if the entitlement were fully exercised` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(j)(ii) claimant B has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks claimant B intends to claim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(j)(iii) claimant B has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks in respect of which Y intends to claim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(k) claimant B has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the period or periods during which claimant B intends to claim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(l)(i) a notice under paragraph (j) or (k) is given by such time as may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(l)(ii) a notice under paragraph (j) or (k) satisfies prescribed conditions as to form and content` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(m) Y consents to the extent of claimant B's intended claim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(n) it is claimant B's intention to care for the child during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to claimant B` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(o) claimant B is absent from work during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to claimant B` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(p) the person is an employee within the meaning of the Employment Rights Act 1996` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(p) claimant B's absence from work during each such week is absence on shared parental leave` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 171ZV(4) "The conditions are": every paragraph must be satisfied.  (f)/(g)-type paragraphs that bite only "if regulations so provide"
-- and the "where ... an employee" paragraph are read as: no such regulation (or not an employee) means nothing to fail.
-- src:3839 | (4) The conditions are—
-- src:3840 | (a) that claimant B and another person (“Y”) who is a person with whom a child is, or is expected to be, placed for adoption under the law of any part of the United Kingdom satisfy prescribed conditions as to caring or intending to care for the child;
-- src:3841 | (b) that claimant B satisfies—
-- src:3842 | (i) prescribed conditions as to relationship with the child, or
-- src:3843 | (ii) prescribed conditions as to relationship with Y;
-- src:3844 | (c) that Y satisfies prescribed conditions—
-- src:3845 | (i) as to employment or self-employment, and
-- src:3846 | (ii) as to having earnings of a prescribed amount for a prescribed period;
-- src:3847 | (d) that claimant B has been in employed earner's employment with an employer for a continuous period of at least the prescribed length ending with a prescribed week;
-- src:3848 | (e) that at the end of that prescribed week claimant B was entitled to be in that employment;
-- src:3849 | (f) that claimant B's normal weekly earnings for a prescribed period ending with a prescribed week are not less than the lower earnings limit in force under section 5(1)(a) at the end of that week;
-- src:3850 | (g) if regulations so provide, that claimant B continues in employed earner's employment (whether or not with the employer by reference to whom the condition in paragraph (d) is satisfied) until a prescribed time;
-- src:3851 | (h) that Y became entitled to statutory adoption pay by reference to the placement for adoption of the child;
-- src:3852 | (i) that Y satisfies prescribed conditions as to the reduction of the duration of the adoption pay period;
-- src:3853 | (j) that claimant B has given the person who will be liable to pay statutory shared parental pay to claimant B notice of—
-- src:3854 | (i) the number of weeks in respect of which claimant B would be entitled to claim statutory shared parental pay in respect of the child if the entitlement were fully exercised (disregarding for these purposes any intention of Y to claim statutory shared parental pay in respect of the child),
-- src:3855 | (ii) the number of weeks in respect of which claimant B intends to claim statutory shared parental pay, and
-- src:3856 | (iii) the number of weeks in respect of which Y intends to claim statutory shared parental pay;
-- src:3857 | (k) that claimant B has given the person who will be liable to pay statutory shared parental pay to claimant B notice of the period or periods during which claimant B intends to claim statutory shared parental pay in respect of the child;
-- src:3858 | (l) that a notice under paragraph (j) or (k)—
-- src:3859 | (i) is given by such time as may be prescribed, and
-- src:3860 | (ii) satisfies prescribed conditions as to form and content;
-- src:3861 | (m) that Y consents to the extent of claimant B's intended claim for statutory shared parental pay;
-- src:3862 | (n) that it is claimant B's intention to care for the child during each week in respect of which statutory shared parental pay is paid to claimant B;
-- src:3863 | (o) that claimant B is absent from work during each week in respect of which statutory shared parental pay is paid to claimant B;
-- src:3864 | (p) that, where claimant B is an employee within the meaning of the Employment Rights Act 1996, claimant B's absence from work during each such week is absence on shared parental leave.
@ref s 171ZV(4) (src:3839-3864)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 171ZV(4) the claimant B's case`
      `s 5(1)(a) the lower earnings limit in force at the time in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 171ZV(4) all the conditions are satisfied` MEANS
        (facts's `(a) claimant B and Y satisfy prescribed conditions as to caring or intending to care for the child`)   -- (a)
    AND ((facts's `(b)(i) claimant B satisfies prescribed conditions as to relationship with the child`) OR (facts's `(b)(ii) claimant B satisfies prescribed conditions as to relationship with Y`))   -- (b)
    AND (facts's `(c)(i) Y satisfies prescribed conditions as to employment or self-employment`) AND (facts's `(c)(ii) Y satisfies prescribed conditions as to having earnings of a prescribed amount for a prescribed period`)   -- (c)
    AND (facts's `(d) weeks of continuous employment ending with the prescribed week`) AT LEAST (facts's `(d) the prescribed length of continuous employment in weeks`)   -- (d)
    AND (facts's `(e) at the end of that prescribed week claimant B was entitled to be in that employment`)   -- (e)
    AND (facts's `(f) normal weekly earnings in pounds for the prescribed period ending with the prescribed week`) AT LEAST `s 5(1)(a) the lower earnings limit in force at the time in pounds`   -- (f)
    AND ((NOT (facts's `(g) regulations so provide that the person continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time`)) OR (facts's `(g) claimant B continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time`))   -- (g)
    AND (facts's `(h) Y became entitled to statutory adoption pay by reference to the placement for adoption of the child`)   -- (h)
    AND (facts's `(i) Y satisfies prescribed conditions as to the reduction of the duration of the adoption pay period`)   -- (i)
    AND (facts's `(j)(i) claimant B has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks claimant B would be entitled to claim if the entitlement were fully exercised`) AND (facts's `(j)(ii) claimant B has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks claimant B intends to claim`) AND (facts's `(j)(iii) claimant B has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks in respect of which Y intends to claim`)   -- (j)
    AND (facts's `(k) claimant B has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the period or periods during which claimant B intends to claim`)   -- (k)
    AND (facts's `(l)(i) a notice under paragraph (j) or (k) is given by such time as may be prescribed`) AND (facts's `(l)(ii) a notice under paragraph (j) or (k) satisfies prescribed conditions as to form and content`)   -- (l)
    AND (facts's `(m) Y consents to the extent of claimant B's intended claim`)   -- (m)
    AND (facts's `(n) it is claimant B's intention to care for the child during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to claimant B`)   -- (n)
    AND (facts's `(o) claimant B is absent from work during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to claimant B`)   -- (o)
    AND ((NOT (facts's `(p) the person is an employee within the meaning of the Employment Rights Act 1996`)) OR (facts's `(p) claimant B's absence from work during each such week is absence on shared parental leave`))   -- (p)

-- s 171ZV(3): "Regulations may provide that, where all the conditions in 171ZV(4) are satisfied ... is to be entitled".
-- READING B (fork F1): the Act states the conditions and the entitlement exists as the regulations provide.  The gate
-- `regulations under s 171ZV(3) provide that claimant B is entitled where the conditions in subsection (4) are satisfied` is an input; if it is false, or if regulations under s 171ZW(1)(a) disapply or modify
-- a condition in the person's case, the text alone cannot answer.  A failed "where" is counted as the text's no (reading (a), for a lawyer).
-- src:3838 | (3) Regulations may provide that, where all the conditions in subsection (4) are satisfied in relation to a person (“claimant B”), claimant B is to be entitled in accordance with the following provisions of this Part to payments to be known as “statutory shared parental pay”.
@ref s 171ZV(3) (src:3838)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 171ZV(4) the claimant B's case`
      `s 5(1)(a) the lower earnings limit in force at the time in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `regulations under s 171ZV(3) provide that claimant B is entitled where the conditions in subsection (4) are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 171ZW(1)(a) regulations disapply or modify a condition in the claimant B's case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZV(3) claimant B is entitled to statutory shared parental pay` MEANS
    IF NOT `regulations under s 171ZV(3) provide that claimant B is entitled where the conditions in subsection (4) are satisfied`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Regulations may provide that" -- the entitlement exists only as regulations provide
    ELSE IF `s 171ZW(1)(a) regulations disapply or modify a condition in the claimant B's case`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 171ZW(1)(a) lets regulations disapply or modify the conditions in prescribed cases
         ELSE IF `s 171ZV(4) all the conditions are satisfied` facts `s 5(1)(a) the lower earnings limit in force at the time in pounds`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Regulations may provide that, where all the conditions in subsection (4) are satisfied in relation to a person (“claimant B”), claimant B is to be entitled" (a failed "where"; reading (a))



-- (5) Regulations may provide for the determination of the extent of entitlement and for when the pay is payable:
-- a power, nothing to encode.

-- (7) "In subsection (6)(a) 'relevant week' means a week falling before the week in which a person takes action that is treated by
-- regulations as constituting for the purposes of this section the person's return to work, and for these purposes 'week' has the
-- meaning given by section 171ZN(8)": seven days beginning with the day of the week on which the adoption pay period begins (the
-- core's fourth week convention).  Only whole weeks before the week of the action count.
-- src:3873 | (7) In subsection (6)(a) “relevant week” means a week falling before the week in which a person takes action that is treated by regulations as constituting for the purposes of this section the person's return to work, and for these purposes “week” has the meaning given by section 171ZN(8).
@ref s 171ZV(7) (src:3873)
GIVEN period IS A Period
      action IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 171ZV(7) the number of relevant weeks of statutory adoption pay` MEANS
    IF action AT MOST period's `the first day`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF wholeWeeksBefore GREATER THAN weeksInPeriod THEN weeksInPeriod ELSE wholeWeeksBefore
    WHERE
        wholeWeeksBefore MEANS FLOOR (((Day action) MINUS (Day (period's `the first day`))) DIVIDED BY 7)
        weeksInPeriod MEANS FLOOR ((((Day (period's `the last day`)) MINUS (Day (period's `the first day`))) PLUS 1) DIVIDED BY 7)

-- (8)(b) "In determining the number of weeks for the purposes of subsection (6)(b) ... a part of a week is to be treated as a week."
-- src:3874 | (8) In determining the number of weeks for the purposes of subsection (6)(b)—
-- src:3875 | (a) “week” has the same meaning as in subsection (7), and
-- src:3876 | (b) a part of a week is to be treated as a week.
@ref s 171ZV(8) (src:3874-3876)
GIVEN weeks IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 171ZV(8) the number of weeks counting a part of a week as a week` MEANS
    CEILING weeks

-- (6) "Provision under subsection (5)(a) is to secure that the number of weeks in respect of which a person is entitled to payments of
-- statutory shared parental pay in respect of a child does not exceed the number of weeks of the adoption pay period reduced by (a)
-- where the person who became entitled to receive statutory adoption pay takes action that is treated by regulations as constituting
-- ... the person's return to work without satisfying conditions prescribed under subsection (2)(h) or (4)(i) (i) the number of
-- relevant weeks in respect of which statutory adoption pay is payable to the person, or (ii) if that number of relevant weeks is
-- less than a number prescribed by regulations, that prescribed number of weeks, or (b) except where paragraph (a) applies, the
-- number of weeks to which the adoption pay period has been reduced by virtue of section 171ZN(2A)."
-- src:3868 | (6) Provision under subsection (5)(a) is to secure that the number of weeks in respect of which a person is entitled to payments of statutory shared parental pay in respect of a child does not exceed the number of weeks of the adoption pay period reduced by—
-- src:3869 | (a) where the person who became entitled to receive statutory adoption pay takes action that is treated by regulations as constituting for the purposes of this section the person's return to work without satisfying conditions prescribed under subsection (2)(h) or, as the case may be, subsection (4)(i)—
-- src:3870 | (i) the number of relevant weeks in respect of which statutory adoption pay is payable to the person, or
-- src:3871 | (ii) if that number of relevant weeks is less than a number prescribed by regulations, that prescribed number of weeks, or
-- src:3872 | (b) except where paragraph (a) applies, the number of weeks to which the adoption pay period has been reduced by virtue of section 171ZN(2A).
@ref s 171ZV(6) (src:3868-3872)
GIVEN `s 171ZN(2) the adoption pay period` IS A Period
      `the person takes action treated by regulations as the person's return to work without satisfying the conditions prescribed under subsection (2)(h) or (4)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of relevant weeks in respect of which statutory adoption pay is payable to the person` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of weeks prescribed by regulations` IS A NUMBER
      `s 171ZN(2A) the number of weeks to which the adoption pay period has been reduced` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 171ZV(6) the greatest number of weeks of statutory shared parental pay` MEANS
    IF cap AT LEAST 0
    THEN JUST cap
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the reduction would exceed the weeks of the period, and the text does not say what then
    WHERE
        apperiod MEANS `s 171ZN(2) the adoption pay period`
        base MEANS (((Day (apperiod's `the last day`)) MINUS (Day (apperiod's `the first day`))) PLUS 1) DIVIDED BY 7
        reduction MEANS
            IF `the person takes action treated by regulations as the person's return to work without satisfying the conditions prescribed under subsection (2)(h) or (4)(i)`
            THEN (IF `the number of relevant weeks in respect of which statutory adoption pay is payable to the person` LESS THAN `the number of weeks prescribed by regulations`
                  THEN `the number of weeks prescribed by regulations`
                  ELSE `the number of relevant weeks in respect of which statutory adoption pay is payable to the person`)
            ELSE `s 171ZV(8) the number of weeks counting a part of a week as a week` `s 171ZN(2A) the number of weeks to which the adoption pay period has been reduced`
        cap MEANS base MINUS reduction

-- (9) "Provision under subsection (5)(a) is to secure that, where two persons are entitled ..., the extent of one's entitlement and the
-- extent of the other's entitlement do not, taken together, exceed what would be available to one person (see subsection (6))."
-- src:3877 | (9) Provision under subsection (5)(a) is to secure that, where two persons are entitled to payments of statutory shared parental pay in respect of a child, the extent of one's entitlement and the extent of the other's entitlement do not, taken together, exceed what would be available to one person (see subsection (6)).
@ref s 171ZV(9) (src:3877)
GIVEN `the weeks of one person's entitlement` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of the other person's entitlement` IS A NUMBER
      `the greatest number of weeks available to one person` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZV(9) the two entitlements together are within what is available to one person` MEANS
    IF `the weeks of one person's entitlement` PLUS `the weeks of the other person's entitlement` AT MOST `the greatest number of weeks available to one person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the extent of one's entitlement and the extent of the other's entitlement do not, taken together, exceed what would be available to one person"

-- (10) "no payment of statutory shared parental pay may be made to a person in respect of a child after the end of such period as may be prescribed."
-- src:3878 | (10) Provision under subsection (5)(b) is to secure that no payment of statutory shared parental pay may be made to a person in respect of a child after the end of such period as may be prescribed.
@ref s 171ZV(10) (src:3878)
GIVEN `the day of the payment` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period prescribed by regulations` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZV(10) a payment may be made in respect of the child` MEANS
    IF `the day of the payment` GREATER THAN `the last day of the period prescribed by regulations`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no payment of statutory shared parental pay may be made to a person in respect of a child after the end of such period as may be prescribed"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a payment within the prescribed period is not barred here, and whether it is payable is for the other provisions

-- (11) "no payment of statutory shared parental pay in respect of a child may be made to a person who became entitled to receive
-- statutory adoption pay in respect of the child before the end of the person's adoption pay period."  A payment on the last day of
-- the period is before the end of the period, which ends with that day.
-- src:3879 | (11) Provision under subsection (5)(b) is to secure that no payment of statutory shared parental pay in respect of a child may be made to a person who became entitled to receive statutory adoption pay in respect of the child before the end of the person's adoption pay period.
@ref s 171ZV(11) (src:3879)
GIVEN `the day of the payment` IS A DATE
      `s 171ZN(2) the adoption pay period` IS A Period
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZV(11) a payment may be made to the person who became entitled to statutory adoption pay` MEANS
    IF `the day of the payment` AT MOST apperiod's `the last day`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no payment of statutory shared parental pay in respect of a child may be made to a person who became entitled to receive statutory adoption pay in respect of the child before the end of the person's adoption pay period"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): after the adoption pay period the bar no longer applies, and whether the pay is payable is for the other provisions
    WHERE apperiod MEANS `s 171ZN(2) the adoption pay period`

-- (13) the conditions for varying the period or periods; (12) the permission.
-- src:3881 | (13) The conditions are—
-- src:3882 | (a) that V has given the person who will be liable to pay statutory shared parental pay to V notice of an intention to vary the period or periods during which V intends to claim statutory shared parental pay;
-- src:3883 | (b) that a notice under paragraph (a)—
-- src:3884 | (i) is given by such time as may be prescribed, and
-- src:3885 | (ii) satisfies prescribed conditions as to form and content.
@ref s 171ZV(13) (src:3881-3885)
GIVEN `V has given notice of an intention to vary the period or periods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is given by the prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice satisfies the prescribed conditions as to form and content` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 171ZV(13) the conditions for varying the period or periods are satisfied` MEANS
        `V has given notice of an intention to vary the period or periods`
    AND `the notice is given by the prescribed time`
    AND `the notice satisfies the prescribed conditions as to form and content`

-- src:3880 | (12) Regulations may provide that, where the conditions in subsection (13) are satisfied in relation to a person who is entitled to statutory shared parental pay under subsection (1) or (3) (“V”), V may vary the period or periods during which V intends to claim statutory shared parental pay in respect of the child in question, subject to complying with provision under subsection (14) where that is relevant.
@ref s 171ZV(12) (src:3880)
GIVEN `regulations under subsection (12) provide for the variation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions in subsection (13) are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZV(12) V may vary the period or periods` MEANS
    IF NOT `regulations under subsection (12) provide for the variation`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Regulations may provide that"
    ELSE IF `the conditions in subsection (13) are satisfied`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the conditions in subsection (13) are satisfied ... V may vary" (a failed "where"; reading (a))

-- (15) the conditions for varying the number of weeks (the person who is X or, as the case may be, Y consents); (14) the permission.
-- src:3887 | (15) The conditions are—
-- src:3888 | (a) that V has given the person who will be liable to pay statutory shared parental pay to V notice of—
-- src:3889 | (i) the extent to which V has exercised an entitlement to statutory shared parental pay in respect of the child,
-- src:3890 | (ii) the extent to which V intends to claim statutory shared parental pay in respect of the child,
-- src:3891 | (iii) the extent to which another person has exercised an entitlement to statutory shared parental pay in respect of the child, and
-- src:3892 | (iv) the extent to which another person intends to claim statutory shared parental pay in respect of the child;
-- src:3893 | (b) that a notice under paragraph (a)—
-- src:3894 | (i) is given by such time as may be prescribed, and
-- src:3895 | (ii) satisfies prescribed conditions as to form and content;
-- src:3896 | (c) that the person who is X or, as the case may be, Y in relation to V consents to that variation.
@ref s 171ZV(15) (src:3887-3896)
GIVEN `V has given notice of the extent to which V has exercised an entitlement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `V has given notice of the extent to which V intends to claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `V has given notice of the extent to which another person has exercised an entitlement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `V has given notice of the extent to which another person intends to claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is given by the prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice satisfies the prescribed conditions as to form and content` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person who is X or, as the case may be, Y in relation to V consents to the variation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 171ZV(15) the conditions for varying the number of weeks are satisfied` MEANS
        `V has given notice of the extent to which V has exercised an entitlement`
    AND `V has given notice of the extent to which V intends to claim`
    AND `V has given notice of the extent to which another person has exercised an entitlement`
    AND `V has given notice of the extent to which another person intends to claim`
    AND `the notice is given by the prescribed time`
    AND `the notice satisfies the prescribed conditions as to form and content`
    AND `the person who is X or, as the case may be, Y in relation to V consents to the variation`

-- src:3886 | (14) Regulations may provide that, where the conditions in subsection (15) are satisfied in relation to a person who is entitled to statutory shared parental pay under subsection (1) or (3) (“V”), V may vary the number of weeks in respect of which V intends to claim statutory shared parental pay.
@ref s 171ZV(14) (src:3886)
GIVEN `regulations under subsection (14) provide for the variation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions in subsection (15) are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZV(14) V may vary the number of weeks` MEANS
    IF NOT `regulations under subsection (14) provide for the variation`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Regulations may provide that"
    ELSE IF `the conditions in subsection (15) are satisfied`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the conditions in subsection (15) are satisfied ... V may vary" (a failed "where"; reading (a))

-- (16) "A person's entitlement to statutory shared parental pay under this section is not affected by the placement for adoption of
-- more than one child as part of the same arrangement."  The answer is the same for one child or several.
-- src:3897 | (16) A person's entitlement to statutory shared parental pay under this section is not affected by the placement for adoption of more than one child as part of the same arrangement.
@ref s 171ZV(16) (src:3897)
GIVEN `the person is entitled under subsection (1) or (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the number of children placed for adoption as part of the same arrangement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZV(16) the entitlement after the placement for adoption of more than one child` MEANS
    IF `the number of children placed for adoption as part of the same arrangement` AT LEAST 1
    THEN `the person is entitled under subsection (1) or (3)`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): there is no placement to speak of

-- (17) Regulations are to provide for entitlement in respect of a child placed under section 22C of the Children Act 1989 (England) or
-- section 81 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014 with a local authority foster parent approved as a prospective
-- adopter: an instruction to the maker of regulations, nothing to encode here (the reading rule in (18) is encoded).

-- (18) "This section has effect in relation to regulations made by virtue of subsection (17) as if (a) references to a child being
-- placed for adoption under the law of any part of the United Kingdom were references to being placed under section 22C of the
-- Children Act 1989 or section 81 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014 with a local authority foster parent who
-- has been approved as a prospective adopter; (b) references to a placement for adoption were references to placement under [either
-- section] with such a person."  An ordinary placement for adoption is one already; the two foster placements count only for
-- regulations made by virtue of (17), and only with an approved foster parent.
-- src:3902 | (18) This section has effect in relation to regulations made by virtue of subsection (17) as if—
-- src:3903 | (a) references to a child being placed for adoption under the law of any part of the United Kingdom were references to being placed under section 22C of the Children Act 1989 or section 81 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014 with a local authority foster parent who has been approved as a prospective adopter;
-- src:3904 | (b) references to a placement for adoption were references to placement under section 22C of the Children Act 1989 or section 81 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014 with such a person.
@ref s 171ZV(18) (src:3902-3904)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of placement`
      `with a local authority foster parent who has been approved as a prospective adopter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulations are made by virtue of subsection (17)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZV(18) the placement counts as a placement for adoption` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `placed for adoption under the law of a part of the United Kingdom` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `placed under section 22C of the Children Act 1989` THEN foster
    WHEN `placed under section 81 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014` THEN foster
    WHERE
        foster MEANS
            IF `the regulations are made by virtue of subsection (17)` AND `with a local authority foster parent who has been approved as a prospective adopter`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the reading applies to "regulations made by virtue of subsection (17)" and to a placement with an approved foster parent

§§ `s 171ZW Entitlement: general`

-- (1)(a) "Regulations may (a) provide that the following do not have effect, or have effect subject to prescribed modifications,
-- in such cases as may be prescribed: (i) section 171ZU(2)(a) to (o) ... (viii) section 171ZV(15)(a) to (c)."
-- The conditions of ss 171ZU and 171ZV are encoded as the Act states them.  This function says what regulations under this power
-- do to one of them in a case.  The other paragraphs of subsection (1) are powers (inert, machinery) and are recorded in NOTES.
-- src:3906 | (1) Regulations may—
-- src:3907 | (a) provide that the following do not have effect, or have effect subject to prescribed modifications, in such cases as may be prescribed—
-- src:3908 | (i) section 171ZU(2)(a) to (o),
-- src:3909 | (ii) section 171ZU(4)(a) to (p),
-- src:3910 | (iii) section 171ZU(13)(a) and (b),
-- src:3911 | (iv) section 171ZU(15)(a) to (c),
-- src:3912 | (v) section 171ZV(2)(a) to (o),
-- src:3913 | (vi) section 171ZV(4)(a) to (p),
-- src:3914 | (vii) section 171ZV(13)(a) and (b), and
-- src:3915 | (viii) section 171ZV(15)(a) to (c);
@ref s 171ZW(1)(a) (src:3906-3915)
GIVEN `regulations provide that the condition does not have effect in the case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulations provide that the condition has effect subject to prescribed modifications in the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZW(1)(a) the condition has effect in the case` MEANS
    IF `regulations provide that the condition does not have effect in the case`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provide that the following do not have effect" in such cases as may be prescribed
    ELSE IF `regulations provide that the condition has effect subject to prescribed modifications in the case`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "have effect subject to prescribed modifications"
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no regulations under this power touch the condition, so it is for section 171ZU or 171ZV

-- (2) "The persons upon whom requirements may be imposed by virtue of subsection (1)(b) include (a) a person who, in connection
-- with another person's claim to be paid statutory shared parental pay, is required to satisfy conditions prescribed under section
-- 171ZU(2)(b) or (4)(c) or 171ZV(2)(b) or (4)(c); (b) an employer or former employer of such a person."  "Include" does not close the list.
-- src:3926 | (2) The persons upon whom requirements may be imposed by virtue of subsection (1)(b) include—
-- src:3927 | (a) a person who, in connection with another person's claim to be paid statutory shared parental pay, is required to satisfy conditions prescribed under section 171ZU(2)(b) or (4)(c) or 171ZV(2)(b) or (4)(c);
-- src:3928 | (b) an employer or former employer of such a person.
@ref s 171ZW(2) (src:3926-3928)
GIVEN `the person is required, in connection with another person's claim, to satisfy conditions prescribed under section 171ZU(2)(b) or (4)(c) or 171ZV(2)(b) or (4)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an employer or former employer of such a person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZW(2) requirements about evidence and procedure may be imposed on the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is required, in connection with another person's claim, to satisfy conditions prescribed under section 171ZU(2)(b) or (4)(c) or 171ZV(2)(b) or (4)(c)`
       OR `the person is an employer or former employer of such a person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include" adds two cases and does not close the list of persons

-- (3) "In subsection (1)(d) 'the prescribed period' means the period of the length prescribed by regulations under section
-- 171ZU(2)(c) or (4)(d) or 171ZV(2)(c) or (4)(d), as the case may be."  The four lengths are inputs; the case picks one.
DECLARE `s 171ZW(3) provision under which the length is prescribed` IS ONE OF
    `s 171ZW(3) section 171ZU(2)(c)`
    `s 171ZW(3) section 171ZU(4)(d)`
    `s 171ZW(3) section 171ZV(2)(c)`
    `s 171ZW(3) section 171ZV(4)(d)`

-- src:3929 | (3) In subsection (1)(d) “the prescribed period” means the period of the length prescribed by regulations under section 171ZU(2)(c) or (4)(d) or 171ZV(2)(c) or (4)(d), as the case may be.
@ref s 171ZW(3) (src:3929)
GIVEN provision IS A `s 171ZW(3) provision under which the length is prescribed`
      `the length prescribed under section 171ZU(2)(c) in weeks` IS A NUMBER
      `the length prescribed under section 171ZU(4)(d) in weeks` IS A NUMBER
      `the length prescribed under section 171ZV(2)(c) in weeks` IS A NUMBER
      `the length prescribed under section 171ZV(4)(d) in weeks` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 171ZW(3) the prescribed period in weeks` MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `s 171ZW(3) section 171ZU(2)(c)` THEN `the length prescribed under section 171ZU(2)(c) in weeks`
    WHEN `s 171ZW(3) section 171ZU(4)(d)` THEN `the length prescribed under section 171ZU(4)(d) in weeks`
    WHEN `s 171ZW(3) section 171ZV(2)(c)` THEN `the length prescribed under section 171ZV(2)(c) in weeks`
    WHEN `s 171ZW(3) section 171ZV(4)(d)` THEN `the length prescribed under section 171ZV(4)(d) in weeks`

§§ `s 171ZX Liability to make payments`

-- (1) "The liability to make payments of statutory shared parental pay under section 171ZU or 171ZV is a liability of any person
-- of whom the person entitled to the payments has been an employee as mentioned in section 171ZU(2)(c) or (4)(d) or 171ZV(2)(c) or (4)(d)."
-- The list of persons is not closed: subsection (3) lets regulations make the Commissioners liable instead.
-- src:3931 | (1) The liability to make payments of statutory shared parental pay under section 171ZU or 171ZV is a liability of any person of whom the person entitled to the payments has been an employee as mentioned in section 171ZU(2)(c) or (4)(d) or 171ZV(2)(c) or (4)(d), as the case may be.
@ref s 171ZX(1) (src:3931)
GIVEN `the person entitled has been an employee of this person as mentioned in s 171ZU(2)(c) or (4)(d) or s 171ZV(2)(c) or (4)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZX(1) the person is liable to make payments of statutory shared parental pay` MEANS
    IF `the person entitled has been an employee of this person as mentioned in s 171ZU(2)(c) or (4)(d) or s 171ZV(2)(c) or (4)(d)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the liability is "a liability of any person of whom" the entitled person has been an employee; s 171ZX(3) lets regulations make the Commissioners liable

-- The same duty as a regulative rule.  The text gives no time limit and no consequence of default, so none is invented.
DECLARE `s 171ZX Party` IS ONE OF
    `s 171ZX the person liable to make the payments`

DECLARE `s 171ZX Action` IS ONE OF
    `s 171ZX makes a payment of statutory shared parental pay` HAS amount IS A NUMBER

-- src:3931 | (1) The liability to make payments of statutory shared parental pay under section 171ZU or 171ZV is a liability of any person of whom the person entitled to the payments has been an employee as mentioned in section 171ZU(2)(c) or (4)(d) or 171ZV(2)(c) or (4)(d), as the case may be.
@ref s 171ZX(1) (src:3931)
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 171ZX Party` `s 171ZX Action`
`s 171ZX(1) the duty to make the payments` MEANS
    PARTY `s 171ZX the person liable to make the payments`
    MUST `s 171ZX makes a payment of statutory shared parental pay` amount
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- (2) Regulations must make provision as to a former employer's liability where the contract was ended to avoid the liability: an
-- instruction to the maker of regulations (inert, machinery; see NOTES).  (3) The Secretary of State's power to make the Commissioners liable: inert, machinery.

§§ `s 171ZY Rate and period of pay`

-- (1) "payable at such fixed or earnings-related weekly rate as may be prescribed by regulations".  The Act gives no figure.
-- src:3935 | (1) Statutory shared parental pay is payable at such fixed or earnings-related weekly rate as may be prescribed by regulations, which may prescribe different kinds of rate for different cases.
@ref s 171ZY(1) (src:3935)
GIVEN `the weekly rate prescribed by regulations for the person's case, in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 171ZY(1) the weekly rate of statutory shared parental pay in pounds` MEANS
    `the weekly rate prescribed by regulations for the person's case, in pounds`   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) when the prescribed rate is not given

-- (7) "a week falls within a relevant period if it falls within a period specified in a notice under (a) section 171ZU(2)(j), (4)(k)
-- or (13)(a), or (b) section 171ZV(2)(j), (4)(k) or (13)(a), and is not afterwards excluded from such a period by a variation of the
-- period or periods during which the person in question intends to claim".
-- src:3943 | (7) For the purposes of this section a week falls within a relevant period if it falls within a period specified in a notice under—
-- src:3944 | (a) section 171ZU(2)(j), (4)(k) or (13)(a), or
-- src:3945 | (b) section 171ZV(2)(j), (4)(k) or (13)(a),
-- src:3946 | and is not afterwards excluded from such a period by a variation of the period or periods during which the person in question intends to claim statutory shared parental pay.
@ref s 171ZY(7) (src:3943-3946)
GIVEN `the week falls within a period specified in a notice under one of the listed paragraphs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the week is afterwards excluded from such a period by a variation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZY(7) the week falls within a relevant period` MEANS
    IF `the week falls within a period specified in a notice under one of the listed paragraphs`
    THEN (IF `the week is afterwards excluded from such a period by a variation`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and is not afterwards excluded from such a period by a variation" (a failed "if"; reading (a))
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a week counts "if it falls within a period specified in a notice", and a week outside every specified period is not covered by that "if"

-- (8) "In this section 'week', in relation to a relevant period, means a period of seven days beginning with the day of the week on
-- which the relevant period starts."  The weeks of a relevant period run from its first day, seven days at a time.
-- src:3947 | (8) In this section “week”, in relation to a relevant period, means a period of seven days beginning with the day of the week on which the relevant period starts.
@ref s 171ZY(8) (src:3947)
GIVEN relevant IS A Period
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE Period
`s 171ZY(8) the week of the relevant period containing the day` MEANS
    IF day LESS THAN relevant's `the first day` OR day GREATER THAN relevant's `the last day`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "'week', in relation to a relevant period"; a day outside the relevant period is not in one of its weeks
    ELSE JUST (Period WITH
                   `the first day` IS Date weekStart
                   `the last day`  IS Date (weekStart PLUS 6))
    WHERE
        weekStart MEANS (Day (relevant's `the first day`)) PLUS 7 TIMES (FLOOR (((Day day) MINUS (Day (relevant's `the first day`))) DIVIDED BY 7))

-- (2) "Subject to the following provisions of this section, statutory shared parental pay is payable to a person in respect of each
-- week falling within a relevant period, up to the number of weeks determined in the case of that person in accordance with
-- regulations under section 171ZU(5) or 171ZV(5)."  Subsections (3) to (5) cut this back: a caller asks them as well.
-- src:3936 | (2) Subject to the following provisions of this section, statutory shared parental pay is payable to a person in respect of each week falling within a relevant period, up to the number of weeks determined in the case of that person in accordance with regulations under section 171ZU(5) or 171ZV(5).
@ref s 171ZY(2) (src:3936)
GIVEN `s 171ZY(7) the week falls within a relevant period` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the number of this week among the weeks paid to the person, counting it` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of weeks determined in the person's case under regulations under section 171ZU(5) or 171ZV(5)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZY(2) statutory shared parental pay is payable for the week` MEANS
    IF `s 171ZY(7) the week falls within a relevant period` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `the number of this week among the weeks paid to the person, counting it` AT MOST `the number of weeks determined in the person's case under regulations under section 171ZU(5) or 171ZV(5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is for "each week falling within a relevant period, up to the number of weeks determined", and it is "Subject to the following provisions of this section"

-- (3) "Except in such cases as may be prescribed, statutory shared parental pay is not payable to a person in respect of a week
-- falling within a relevant period if it is not the person's intention at the beginning of the week to care for the child by
-- reference to whom the person satisfies (a) the condition in section 171ZU(2)(a) or (4)(a), or (b) the condition in section 171ZV(2)(a) or (4)(a)."
-- src:3937 | (3) Except in such cases as may be prescribed, statutory shared parental pay is not payable to a person in respect of a week falling within a relevant period if it is not the person's intention at the beginning of the week to care for the child by reference to whom the person satisfies—
-- src:3938 | (a) the condition in section 171ZU(2)(a) or (4)(a), or
-- src:3939 | (b) the condition in section 171ZV(2)(a) or (4)(a).
@ref s 171ZY(3) (src:3937-3939)
GIVEN `s 171ZY(7) the week falls within a relevant period` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is the person's intention at the beginning of the week to care for the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is one prescribed by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZY(3) the pay is payable for the week despite the intention to care` MEANS
    IF `the case is one prescribed by regulations`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Except in such cases as may be prescribed"
    ELSE IF `s 171ZY(7) the week falls within a relevant period` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND (NOT `it is the person's intention at the beginning of the week to care for the child`)
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "statutory shared parental pay is not payable to a person in respect of a week falling within a relevant period if it is not the person's intention at the beginning of the week to care for the child"
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a week with the intention to care, or outside a relevant period, is for the grant in subsection (2)

-- (4) "Except in such cases as may be prescribed, statutory shared parental pay is not payable to a person in respect of a week
-- falling within a relevant period during any part of which week the person works for any employer."
-- src:3940 | (4) Except in such cases as may be prescribed, statutory shared parental pay is not payable to a person in respect of a week falling within a relevant period during any part of which week the person works for any employer.
@ref s 171ZY(4) (src:3940)
GIVEN `s 171ZY(7) the week falls within a relevant period` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person works for any employer during any part of the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is one prescribed by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZY(4) the pay is payable for the week despite work for an employer` MEANS
    IF `the case is one prescribed by regulations`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Except in such cases as may be prescribed"
    ELSE IF `s 171ZY(7) the week falls within a relevant period` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the person works for any employer during any part of the week`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "statutory shared parental pay is not payable to a person in respect of a week falling within a relevant period during any part of which week the person works for any employer"
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a week without that work, or outside a relevant period, is for the grant in subsection (2)

-- (5) The Secretary of State's power to specify circumstances of no liability to pay: inert, machinery.

-- (6) "the amount payable by way of statutory shared parental pay for any day shall be taken as one seventh of the weekly rate."
-- src:3942 | (6) Where for any purpose of this Part or of regulations it is necessary to calculate the daily rate of statutory shared parental pay, the amount payable by way of statutory shared parental pay for any day shall be taken as one seventh of the weekly rate.
@ref s 171ZY(6) (src:3942)
GIVEN `the weekly rate in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 171ZY(6) the daily rate in pounds` MEANS
    `the weekly rate in pounds` DIVIDED BY 7

§§ `s 171ZZ Restrictions on contracting out`

-- (1) "An agreement is void to the extent that it purports (a) to exclude, limit or otherwise modify any provision of
-- this Part, or (b) to require a person to contribute ... towards any costs incurred by that person's employer or former
-- employer under this Part."  An agreement that purports neither is not said to be void here.
-- src:3949 | (1) An agreement is void to the extent that it purports—
-- src:3950 | (a) to exclude, limit or otherwise modify any provision of this Part, or
-- src:3951 | (b) to require a person to contribute (whether directly or indirectly) towards any costs incurred by that person's employer or former employer under this Part.
@ref s 171ZZ(1) (src:3949-3951)
GIVEN `the agreement purports to exclude, limit or otherwise modify a provision of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement purports to require a person to contribute towards costs incurred by the person's employer or former employer under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ(1) the agreement is void to that extent` MEANS
    IF `the agreement purports to exclude, limit or otherwise modify a provision of this Part`
       OR `the agreement purports to require a person to contribute towards costs incurred by the person's employer or former employer under this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "void to the extent that it purports" (a) or (b); an agreement that purports neither is not covered by this subsection

-- (2) "For the avoidance of doubt, an agreement between an employer and an employee, authorising deductions from
-- statutory shared parental pay ..., is not void by virtue of subsection (1)(a) if the employer (a) is authorised by that or another agreement to make
-- the same deductions from any contractual remuneration ..., or (b) would be so authorised if the employer were liable to
-- pay contractual remuneration in respect of that period."  A failed "if" is counted as the text's no (reading (a)).
-- src:3952 | (2) For the avoidance of doubt, an agreement between an employer and an employee, authorising deductions from statutory shared parental pay which the employer is liable to pay to the employee in respect of any period, is not void by virtue of subsection (1)(a) if the employer—
-- src:3953 | (a) is authorised by that or another agreement to make the same deductions from any contractual remuneration which the employer is liable to pay in respect of the same period, or
-- src:3954 | (b) would be so authorised if the employer were liable to pay contractual remuneration in respect of that period.
@ref s 171ZZ(2) (src:3952-3954)
GIVEN `the employer is authorised to make the same deductions from contractual remuneration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer would be so authorised if liable to pay contractual remuneration for the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ(2) the agreement authorising deductions is not void by virtue of subsection (1)(a)` MEANS
    IF `the employer is authorised to make the same deductions from contractual remuneration`
       OR `the employer would be so authorised if liable to pay contractual remuneration for the period`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not void by virtue of subsection (1)(a) if the employer" is authorised, or would be (a failed "if"; reading (a))

§§ `s 171ZZ1 Relationship with contractual remuneration`

-- (1) "Subject to subsections (2) and (3), any entitlement to statutory shared parental pay is not to affect any right
-- of a person in relation to remuneration under any contract of service ('contractual remuneration')."
-- Subsection (3) lets regulations decide which payments are contractual remuneration, so if they say otherwise the text alone cannot answer.
-- src:3956 | (1) Subject to subsections (2) and (3), any entitlement to statutory shared parental pay is not to affect any right of a person in relation to remuneration under any contract of service (“contractual remuneration”).
@ref s 171ZZ1(1) (src:3956)
GIVEN `regulations under subsection (3) treat the payment otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ1(1) the entitlement affects the person's right to contractual remuneration` MEANS
    IF `regulations under subsection (3) treat the payment otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsection (3) lets regulations say which payments are, and which are not, contractual remuneration
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any entitlement to statutory shared parental pay is not to affect any right of a person in relation to remuneration under any contract of service"

-- (2)(a) "any contractual remuneration paid to a person by an employer ... in respect of any period is to go towards
-- discharging any liability of that employer to pay statutory shared parental pay to that person in respect of that period".
-- The remuneration paid is net of anything regulations treat as not being contractual remuneration (subsection (3)).
-- src:3958 | (a) any contractual remuneration paid to a person by an employer of that person in respect of any period is to go towards discharging any liability of that employer to pay statutory shared parental pay to that person in respect of that period; and
@ref s 171ZZ1(2)(a) (src:3958)
GIVEN `liability to pay statutory shared parental pay for the period, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `contractual remuneration paid for the same period, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 171ZZ1(2)(a) the liability to pay statutory shared parental pay that remains` MEANS
    IF `contractual remuneration paid for the same period, in pounds` AT LEAST `liability to pay statutory shared parental pay for the period, in pounds`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `liability to pay statutory shared parental pay for the period, in pounds` MINUS `contractual remuneration paid for the same period, in pounds`

-- (2)(b) "any statutory shared parental pay paid by an employer to a person who is an employee of that employer in
-- respect of any period is to go towards discharging any liability of that employer to pay contractual remuneration".
-- src:3959 | (b) any statutory shared parental pay paid by an employer to a person who is an employee of that employer in respect of any period is to go towards discharging any liability of that employer to pay contractual remuneration to that person in respect of that period.
@ref s 171ZZ1(2)(b) (src:3959)
GIVEN `liability to pay contractual remuneration for the period, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `statutory shared parental pay paid for the same period, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 171ZZ1(2)(b) the liability to pay contractual remuneration that remains` MEANS
    IF `statutory shared parental pay paid for the same period, in pounds` AT LEAST `liability to pay contractual remuneration for the period, in pounds`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `liability to pay contractual remuneration for the period, in pounds` MINUS `statutory shared parental pay paid for the same period, in pounds`

§§ `s 171ZZ2 Crown employment`

-- "The provisions of this Part apply in relation to persons employed by or under the Crown as they apply in relation to
-- persons employed otherwise than by or under the Crown."  The answer is the same whoever the employer is.
-- src:3962 | The provisions of this Part apply in relation to persons employed by or under the Crown as they apply in relation to persons employed otherwise than by or under the Crown.
@ref s 171ZZ2 (src:3962)
GIVEN `the kind of employer` IS A `Kind of employer`
      `the provisions of this Part apply to the person if the employer were not the Crown` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ2 the provisions of this Part apply to the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of employer`
    WHEN `an individual` THEN `the provisions of this Part apply to the person if the employer were not the Crown`
    WHEN `a company or other body corporate` THEN `the provisions of this Part apply to the person if the employer were not the Crown`
    WHEN `a government department, public authority or other body of persons` THEN `the provisions of this Part apply to the person if the employer were not the Crown`
    WHEN `the Crown` THEN `the provisions of this Part apply to the person if the employer were not the Crown`

§§ `s 171ZZ3 Special classes of person`

-- (1) "The Secretary of State may with the concurrence of the Treasury make regulations modifying any provision of this Part
-- ... in its application to any person who is, has been or is to be (a) employed on board any ship, vessel, hovercraft or
-- aircraft; (b) outside Great Britain at any prescribed time or in any prescribed circumstances; or (c) in prescribed
-- employment in connection with continental shelf operations, as defined in section 120(2)."
-- This is what the power reaches; the regulations themselves are outside the sources (subsection (2) lists what they may do).
-- src:3964 | (1) The Secretary of State may with the concurrence of the Treasury make regulations modifying any provision of this Part in such manner as the Secretary of State thinks proper in its application to any person who is, has been or is to be—
-- src:3965 | (a) employed on board any ship, vessel, hovercraft or aircraft;
-- src:3966 | (b) outside Great Britain at any prescribed time or in any prescribed circumstances; or
-- src:3967 | (c) in prescribed employment in connection with continental shelf operations, as defined in section 120(2).
@ref s 171ZZ3(1) (src:3964-3967)
GIVEN `the person is employed on board a ship, vessel, hovercraft or aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is outside Great Britain at a prescribed time or in prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is in prescribed employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 120(2) the employment is in connection with continental shelf operations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ3(1) regulations may modify this Part in its application to the person` MEANS
    IF     `the person is employed on board a ship, vessel, hovercraft or aircraft`
        OR `the person is outside Great Britain at a prescribed time or in prescribed circumstances`
        OR (`the person is in prescribed employment` AND `s 120(2) the employment is in connection with continental shelf operations`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is for a person who is, has been or is to be in one of the three classes



§§ `s 171ZZ4 Part 12ZC: supplementary`

-- (1) Definitions that point at another provision.  Each returns what the other provision supplies (the seam is named after it).
-- src:3975 | “adoption pay period” has the meaning given in section 171ZN(2);
@ref s 171ZZ4(1) (src:3975)
GIVEN `s 171ZN(2) the adoption pay period` IS A Period
GIVETH A Period
`s 171ZZ4(1) adoption pay period` MEANS `s 171ZN(2) the adoption pay period`

-- src:3983 | “maternity allowance period” has the meaning given in section 35(2);
@ref s 171ZZ4(1) (src:3983)
GIVEN `s 35(2) the maternity allowance period` IS A Period
GIVETH A Period
